  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1... \nA dry period continues to be the case in the forecast. Sunday\nwill feature a shortwave beginning to move into the region but\nwill be well to the north of the forecast area. Thus, a dry\nforecast will be in place. Cloud cover is expected ahead of the\ntrough and will pass through the area through the day before\nclearing out after 00Z Monday. This will impact daytime\ntemperatures as well as the fog potential for Sunday night. \n\nThe rest of the work week features the column slowing warming \nand mid level heights building. High temps climb back above \nseasonal values with 70s common outside of the higher elevations\nThursday through next weekend. We may have a shot at our second\n80F degree day of the month next weekend with probs climbing \ninto the 30 percentile range and the forecast 50th percentile a \nfew degrees higher in most recent runs. \n\nFrost advisories are likely in the northeast and southeast\ncorners of our area Tuesday morning and perhaps Wednesday as \nwell. There is more confidence in Tuesday at sunrise given the \nlocation of the surface anticyclone. Probs of min temps less \nthan 37 degrees range from 45-80% in the aforementioned areas,\nwhile those numbers drop between 20-30% at daybreak Wednesday. \nThe mean first frost at Dubois airport is September 25th and the\n/late/ 90th percentile is October 9th, thus we are on the later\nside of climo this year.",
